From c0bf74496568e9f0c24ca6a3f41e669d060687b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:57:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm: rz-du: correct the account of the first commit in
 atomic_flush

The comment above the hand-over check in rzg2l_du_crtc_atomic_flush()
says drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm() commits planes before the
modeset enable, so that the first commit is never flushed and the
bootloader's picture survives it.  The helper does the opposite:

  drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_disables()
  drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables()
  drm_atomic_helper_commit_planes()

rzg2l_du_crtc_atomic_enable() clears boot_logo_handover before the
flush runs, so the first commit is flushed like any other and its
planes go on screen at the next frame boundary.  This was confirmed on
the board the hard way: with DRM fbdev emulation enabled, fbdev's own
post-probe hotplug commit put its blank framebuffer up over the logo,
long before the compositor started.

The code is right; only the reasoning was wrong, and it matters,
because the wrong version implies the first commit is free.  It is
not: whoever commits first takes the screen, so nothing in the kernel
may commit before the compositor does.  Say that, and keep the check
for what it actually is - a guard against a flush while the hand-over
is still pending.

No functional change.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G3L boot logo, board specific]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/renesas/rz-du/rzg2l_du_crtc.c | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/renesas/rz-du/rzg2l_du_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/renesas/rz-du/rzg2l_du_crtc.c
index c10b099..846587e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/renesas/rz-du/rzg2l_du_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/renesas/rz-du/rzg2l_du_crtc.c
@@ -363,12 +363,19 @@ static void rzg2l_du_crtc_atomic_flush(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm() commits planes before it enables
-	 * the modeset, so on the very first commit this runs before
-	 * rzg2l_du_vsp_enable() has set the pipeline up.  Flushing here would
-	 * commit a display list built from an empty pipeline and, through
-	 * vsp1_dl_list_hw_enqueue(), overwrite VI6_DL_HDR_ADDR0 - which is the
-	 * register still pointing at the bootloader's self-looping chain.
+	 * drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm() runs the modeset enables before
+	 * it commits planes.  By the time the first commit gets here,
+	 * rzg2l_du_crtc_atomic_enable() has already taken the VSP over and
+	 * cleared the hand-over, so the first commit is flushed like any other
+	 * and its planes replace the bootloader's picture at the next frame
+	 * boundary.  Whoever commits first therefore takes the screen: nothing
+	 * in the kernel may commit before the compositor does.
+	 *
+	 * This check is only a guard.  A flush that ran while the hand-over
+	 * was still pending would commit a display list built from a pipeline
+	 * that has not been set up, and through vsp1_dl_list_hw_enqueue()
+	 * overwrite VI6_DL_HDR_ADDR0 - the register still pointing at the
+	 * bootloader's display list chain.
 	 */
 	if (rcrtc->boot_logo_handover)
 		return;
